
---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";

const photoFolder = "/assets/projects/haverhill/";

const photos = [
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.50 PM (1).jpeg",
    alt: "Complete metal exterior on a custom Kansas home"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.50 PM (2).jpeg",
    alt: "Textured black siding and Ash Gray metal roofing"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.50 PM (3).jpeg",
    alt: "Metal exterior and garage on Haverhill project"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.50 PM (4).jpeg",
    alt: "Covered porch with metal roofing and siding"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.50 PM.jpeg",
    alt: "Custom home metal exterior installation"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.51 PM (1).jpeg",
    alt: "Standing seam metal roof and exterior siding"
  },
  {
    file: "WhatsApp Image 2026-11-02 at 8.06.51 PM.jpeg",
    alt: "Finished metal exterior on Kansas new construction"
  }
];

const photoUrl = (file) =>
  photoFolder + encodeURIComponent(file);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Metal Siding for New Homes in Kansas | Oak Contracting LLC"
  description="Explore complete metal exteriors for new construction homes in Kansas, featuring a real Oak Contracting project with textured standing seam roofing and metal siding."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="article-page">
    <article class="article-container">

      <a class="back-link" href="/blog/">
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>

      <p class="eyebrow">METAL EXTERIORS · KANSAS</p>

      <h1>
        Complete Metal Exteriors for New Construction Homes:
        A Kansas Contractor's Perspective
      </h1>

      <p class="intro">
        A new home's exterior is about more than appearance.
        It's an investment in protection, durability, and
        long-term value. Here's how we approach complete
        metal exterior projects at Oak Contracting LLC.
      </p>

      <img
        class="hero-image"
        src={photoUrl(photos[0].file)}
        alt={photos[0].alt}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />

      <p class="caption">
        Haverhill project near Augusta, Kansas —
        exterior finish completed by Oak Contracting LLC.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Haverhill Project Near Augusta, Kansas</h2>

      <p>
        We recently completed the full exterior finish
        on a new construction home in the Haverhill area
        near Augusta, Kansas.
      </p>

      <p>
        This project demonstrates how different metal
        profiles, finishes, and colors can work together
        to create a distinctive exterior.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Textured Ash Gray standing seam metal roofing</li>
        <li>Textured black metal siding</li>
        <li>Textured black soffit and fascia</li>
        <li>Woodgrain board-and-batten porch accents</li>
        <li>Horizontal corrugated metal garage accents</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The contrast between the Ash Gray roof and black
        siding creates a bold appearance. Woodgrain accents
        introduce warmth, while the horizontal corrugated
        panels add architectural interest.
      </p>

      <div class="photo-grid">
        {photos.slice(1, 3).map((photo) => (
          <img
            src={photoUrl(photo.file)}
            alt={photo.alt}
            loading="lazy"
          />
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Why Choose Metal Siding for a New Home?</h2>

      <p>
        Metal siding isn't limited to agricultural buildings.
        Today's metal products offer a wide range of profiles,
        colors, and finishes for custom residential construction.
      </p>

      <p>
        Homeowners can combine vertical panels, board-and-batten
        styles, horizontal accents, and other exterior materials
        to achieve the appearance they want.
      </p>

      <p>
        When properly selected and installed, metal siding can
        offer excellent durability and long-term performance.
        The right product depends on the home's design,
        budget, and the owner's expectations.
      </p>

      <h2>Does Metal Thickness Matter?</h2>

      <p>
        Generally speaking, heavier-gauge metal can offer
        greater resistance to physical damage. However,
        not every home requires the heaviest available panel.
      </p>

      <p>
        At Oak Contracting, we work with quality metal products
        and help customers choose materials that fit their
        particular project.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes a standard panel is an excellent choice.
        Other times, upgrading to a heavier material or
        different panel system makes sense.
      </p>

      <h2>Textured Metal vs. Smooth Metal</h2>

      <p>
        Both the Ash Gray standing seam roof and black siding
        on our Haverhill project feature textured finishes.
      </p>

      <p>
        Textured metal offers a subdued, matte appearance
        and can help make minor panel waviness, sometimes
        called oil canning, less noticeable.
      </p>

      <p>
        For homeowners who prefer a less reflective exterior,
        textured finishes are worth considering.
      </p>

      <div class="photo-grid">
        {photos.slice(3, 5).map((photo) => (
          <img
            src={photoUrl(photo.file)}
            alt={photo.alt}
            loading="lazy"
          />
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Why Consider Standing Seam Roofing?</h2>

      <p>
        Standing seam roofing uses concealed fastening
        methods rather than exposing the primary panel
        fasteners directly to the weather.
      </p>

      <p>
        This can offer maintenance advantages while
        creating clean architectural lines.
        Proper flashing and installation remain essential.
      </p>

      <p>
        Standing seam generally costs more than traditional
        exposed-fastener metal roofing, so homeowners should
        consider their budget and long-term expectations.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Installation Details Matter</h2>

      <p>
        One of the biggest mistakes we see in building repairs
        is addressing only the visible problem without
        investigating what's happening underneath.
      </p>

      <p>
        Proper preparation, flashing, fastening, and transitions
        are important to the performance of any exterior.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our approach is to understand the building, identify
        potential problems, and address them correctly rather
        than simply covering them up.
      </p>

      <h2>Why We Enjoy Complete Exterior Projects</h2>

      <p>
        Complete exterior projects allow us to focus on
        how every component works together, from the
        roof and siding to the soffit, fascia, and accents.
      </p>

      <p>
        We take pride in handling complicated details
        and delivering work we're proud to put our name on.
      </p>

      <p>
        One of the best compliments we can receive is
        hearing that we made the construction process
        seem easy and that the finished result exceeded
        the customer's expectations.
      </p>

      <div class="photo-grid">
        {photos.slice(5).map((photo) => (
          <img
            src={photoUrl(photo.file)}
            alt={photo.alt}
            loading="lazy"
          />
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Planning a New Home in Central Kansas?</h2>

      <p>
        Oak Contracting LLC specializes in complete metal
        exterior finishes, metal roofing, siding, and
        agricultural and commercial building repairs.
      </p>

      <p>
        Based in Partridge, Kansas, we serve Hutchinson,
        Reno County, and surrounding Central Kansas communities.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-box">
        <h2>Let's Talk About Your Project</h2>
        <p>
          Planning a new home or considering a complete
          metal exterior? We'd welcome the opportunity
          to discuss your project.
        </p>
        <a href="/#contact" class="contact-button">
          Request an Estimate
        </a>
        <a href="tel:+16203143557" class="phone-link">
          Call (620) 314-3557
        </a>
      </div>

    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-page {
    background: #f6f6f4;
    color: #252525;
    padding: 65px 20px 90px;
  }

  .article-container {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 35px;
    color: #555;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #777;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 15px 0 25px;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #555;
  }

  .hero-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-top: 35px;
  }

  .caption {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #777;
    margin: 10px 0 45px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 29px;
    margin: 50px 0 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  p, li {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 25px;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .photo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 15px;
    margin: 35px 0;
  }

  .photo-grid img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 260px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .contact-box {
    background: #25262c;
    color: white;
    padding: 35px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-top: 55px;
  }

  .contact-box h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-block;
    background: white;
    color: #222;
    padding: 13px 20px;
    margin: 15px 15px 10px 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .phone-link {
    color: white;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 15px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .article-page {
      padding: 40px 18px 65px;
    }

    .photo-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .photo-grid img {
      height: auto;
    }

    .contact-box {
      padding: 25px;
    }
  }
</style>
